module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.VeryAmpleAffineBase.AwayFraction
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.VeryAmpleAffineBase.CoordinateCharts

/-!
# The section-value dictionary on a whole degree-zero localization

`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/VeryAmpleAffineBase/SectionDictionary.lean` identifies *one*
coordinate ratio: for a family `s` of global sections of an invertible module attached to
degree-one elements `y_i` of a graded ring `A` through `α : X ⟶ Proj A`, the ratio `s_k / s_i` is
the inverse image along `α` of the degree-zero fraction `y_k / y_i` of `A₍y_i₎`.

The coordinate cut of [Stacks, Tag 02NP] does not consume single ratios. It consumes the chart
generators `b / y_i^D`, which by
`Stacks.AwayFraction.mk_mem_closure_of_mem_adjoin` are *polynomials over `A₀` in the ratios* —
sums of monomials, each a product of several `y_m / y_i`. This file is that generalisation: the
inverse image along `α` of a degree-zero fraction is packaged as a **ring homomorphism**
`A₍y_i₎ ⟶ Γ(X, W)`, so that the one-ratio dictionary propagates through products and sums at no
cost.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.CoordinateDictionary.pullbackAway`: **the inverse image along `α` of a degree-zero
  fraction, as a ring homomorphism** `A₍q₎ ⟶ Γ(X, W)` for `W ≤ α⁻¹(D₊(q))`. On the fraction
  `p / q` it is `Stacks.CoordinateDictionary.pullbackAwayCoord`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.CoordinateDictionary.pullbackAway_awayCoord`: the ring homomorphism agrees with
  `Stacks.CoordinateDictionary.pullbackAwayCoord` on the fractions `p / q`, so the one-ratio
  dictionary is a statement about it.
* `Stacks.CoordinateDictionary.pullbackAway_mk_finsuppProd`: **the dictionary on a product.** The
  inverse image of a monomial of total degree `N` in the coordinates, divided by `y_i^N`, is the
  same monomial in the coordinate ratios `s_m / s_i`.
* `Stacks.CoordinateDictionary.pullbackAway_mk_mem_closure`: **the dictionary on a chart
  generator.** For `b` homogeneous of degree `D` in the subalgebra generated over `A₀` by the
  coordinates, the inverse image of `b / y_i^D` lies in the subring of `Γ(X, W)` generated by the
  inverse images of the degree-zero constants together with the coordinate ratios.

## Implementation notes

Nothing here is an induction. `Stacks.AwayFraction` has already written the fraction `b / y_i^D`
as an element of a `Subring.closure` inside `A₍y_i₎`; a ring homomorphism carries a
`Subring.closure` into the `Subring.closure` of the images of its generators, and the one-ratio
dictionary says what those images are. The only arithmetic is the `Finsupp.prod` bookkeeping of
`Stacks.CoordinateDictionary.pullbackAway_mk_finsuppProd`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02NP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02NP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NA)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace Opposite
open HomogeneousLocalization
open Stacks.ProjectiveFromSections

universe u w

namespace Stacks.CoordinateDictionary

variable {A : Type u} {σ : Type w} [CommRing A] [SetLike σ A] [AddSubgroupClass σ A]
  (𝒜 : ℕ → σ) [GradedRing 𝒜] {X : Scheme.{u}} (α : X ⟶ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒜)

/-! ### The inverse image of a fraction, as a ring homomorphism -/

/-- **The inverse image along `α` of a degree-zero fraction of `A₍q₎`, as a ring
homomorphism.** It is `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.awayToSection` — the identification of `A₍q₎` with
the sections of `𝒪_{Proj A}` over `D₊(q)` — followed by `α` on sections, restricted to an open
`W` of `X` inside `α⁻¹(D₊(q))`. -/
def pullbackAway {q : A} {W : X.Opens}
    (hle : W ≤ α ⁻¹ᵁ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 q) : Away 𝒜 q →+* Γ(X, W) :=
  (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.awayToSection 𝒜 q ≫
    α.appLE (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 q) W hle).hom

/-- **The ring homomorphism computes `Stacks.CoordinateDictionary.pullbackAwayCoord` on the
fractions `p / q`**, so the one-ratio section-value dictionary is a statement about it. -/
theorem pullbackAway_awayCoord {q : A} (hq : q ∈ 𝒜 1) {W : X.Opens}
    (hle : W ≤ α ⁻¹ᵁ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 q) (p : 𝒜 1) :
    pullbackAway 𝒜 α hle (awayCoord 𝒜 hq p) = pullbackAwayCoord 𝒜 α hq hle p :=
  rfl

/-! ### The dictionary on products and on the chart generators -/

section Family

variable {L : X.Modules} [Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X L]

/-- The inverse image of the fraction `y_j / y_i` is the restricted coordinate ratio `s_j / s_i`. -/
private theorem pullbackAway_mk_one_eq_resO (hgen : Algebra.adjoin (𝒜 0) ((𝒜 1 : Set A)) = ⊤)
    (e : pullbackTwistOne 𝒜 α ≅ L) {ι : Type*} (y : ι → 𝒜 1) (s : ι → Γ(L, ⊤))
    (hs : ∀ j, s j = e.hom.app ⊤ (coordSection 𝒜 α (y j))) (i j : ι) {W : X.Opens}
    (hle : W ≤ α ⁻¹ᵁ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 ((y i : A))) :
    pullbackAway 𝒜 α hle (Away.mk 𝒜 (y i).2 1 ((y j : A)) (by simp)) =
      resO (hle.trans (preimage_basicOpen_le_nvCover 𝒜 α hgen e y s hs i)) (ratio s i j) := by
  rw [resO_ratio_eq_pullbackAwayCoord_of_le_preimage 𝒜 α hgen e y s hs i j hle]
  rfl

/-- **The section-value dictionary on a product of coordinate ratios.** A monomial of total
degree `N` in the degree-one coordinates `y`, divided by `y_i^N`, has inverse image along `α` the
same monomial in the coordinate ratios `s_m / s_i`.

`Stacks.AwayFraction.mk_finsuppProd` splits the fraction into a product of the fractions
`y_m / y_i` inside `A₍y_i₎`, the ring homomorphism
`Stacks.CoordinateDictionary.pullbackAway` carries the product to a product, and
`Stacks.CoordinateDictionary.resO_ratio_eq_pullbackAwayCoord_of_le_preimage` identifies each
factor. -/
theorem pullbackAway_mk_finsuppProd (hgen : Algebra.adjoin (𝒜 0) ((𝒜 1 : Set A)) = ⊤)
    (e : pullbackTwistOne 𝒜 α ≅ L) {ι : Type*} (y : ι → 𝒜 1) (s : ι → Γ(L, ⊤))
    (hs : ∀ j, s j = e.hom.app ⊤ (coordSection 𝒜 α (y j))) (i : ι) {W : X.Opens}
    (hle : W ≤ α ⁻¹ᵁ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 ((y i : A)))
    (m : ι →₀ ℕ) {N : ℕ} (hN : N = m.sum fun _ k => k)
    (h : (m.prod fun j k => ((y j : A)) ^ k) ∈ 𝒜 (N • 1)) :
    pullbackAway 𝒜 α hle
        (Away.mk 𝒜 (y i).2 N (m.prod fun j k => ((y j : A)) ^ k) h) =
      m.prod fun j k =>
        resO (hle.trans (preimage_basicOpen_le_nvCover 𝒜 α hgen e y s hs i))
          (ratio s i j) ^ k := by
  rw [Stacks.AwayFraction.mk_finsuppProd 𝒜 (fun j => ((y j : A))) (fun j => (y j).2) i m hN h,
    Finsupp.prod, Finsupp.prod, map_prod]
  refine Finset.prod_congr rfl fun j _ => ?_
  rw [map_pow]
  exact congrArg (· ^ _) (pullbackAway_mk_one_eq_resO 𝒜 α hgen e y s hs i j hle)

/-- **The section-value dictionary on a chart generator of [Stacks, Tag 02NP].** Let `b` be
homogeneous of degree `D` and lie in the subalgebra generated over `A₀` by the degree-one
coordinates `y`. Then the inverse image along `α` of the degree-zero fraction `b / y_i^D` lies in
the subring of `Γ(X, W)` generated by the inverse images of the degree-zero constants together
with the coordinate ratios `s_m / s_i`.

This is the form the surjectivity step of the coordinate cut consumes: the constants come from
the base and the ratios are the coordinates of the pinned morphism to `ℙⁿ_S`, so every generator
of the chart is exhibited as a polynomial in sections that the morphism to projective space
reaches.

`Stacks.AwayFraction.mk_mem_closure_of_mem_adjoin` is the same statement inside `A₍y_i₎`; a ring
homomorphism carries a `Subring.closure` into the closure of the images of its generators, and
`Stacks.CoordinateDictionary.resO_ratio_eq_pullbackAwayCoord_of_le_preimage` says what those
images are. -/
theorem pullbackAway_mk_mem_closure (hgen : Algebra.adjoin (𝒜 0) ((𝒜 1 : Set A)) = ⊤)
    (e : pullbackTwistOne 𝒜 α ≅ L) {ι : Type*} (y : ι → 𝒜 1) (s : ι → Γ(L, ⊤))
    (hs : ∀ j, s j = e.hom.app ⊤ (coordSection 𝒜 α (y j))) (i : ι) {W : X.Opens}
    (hle : W ≤ α ⁻¹ᵁ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 ((y i : A)))
    {D : ℕ} {b : A} (hb : b ∈ 𝒜 D)
    (hbmem : b ∈ Algebra.adjoin (𝒜 0) (Set.range fun j => ((y j : A)))) :
    pullbackAway 𝒜 α hle (Away.mk 𝒜 (y i).2 D b (by simpa using hb)) ∈
      Subring.closure
        (Set.range (fun r : 𝒜 0 => pullbackAway 𝒜 α hle
            (algebraMap (𝒜 0) (Away 𝒜 ((y i : A))) r)) ∪
          Set.range fun k =>
            resO (hle.trans (preimage_basicOpen_le_nvCover 𝒜 α hgen e y s hs i))
              (ratio s i k)) := by
  have h := Subring.mem_closure_image_of (pullbackAway 𝒜 α hle)
    (Stacks.AwayFraction.mk_mem_closure_of_mem_adjoin 𝒜 (fun j => ((y j : A)))
      (fun j => (y j).2) i hb hbmem)
  refine Subring.closure_mono ?_ h
  rintro _ ⟨z, (⟨r, rfl⟩ | ⟨j, rfl⟩), rfl⟩
  · exact Or.inl ⟨r, rfl⟩
  · exact Or.inr ⟨j, (pullbackAway_mk_one_eq_resO 𝒜 α hgen e y s hs i j hle).symm⟩

end Family

end Stacks.CoordinateDictionary

end
